---
---
<section id="faq" class="py-16 md:py-24 border-t border-dark-700/50">
  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6">
    
    <div class="text-center max-w-2xl mx-auto mb-14">
      <h2 class="text-xs font-mono uppercase tracking-wider text-brand-400 font-semibold mb-2">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
      <h3 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-bold text-white tracking-tight">
        Everything You Need to Know
      </h3>
    </div>

    <div class="space-y-6">
      
      <!-- FAQ 1 -->
      <div class="p-6 rounded-2xl bg-dark-800/60 border border-dark-700/80">
        <h4 class="text-base sm:text-lg font-bold text-white mb-2">How does the "Pause or Cancel Anytime" feature work?</h4>
        <p class="text-sm text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
          We understand engineering workloads fluctuate. If you complete a major release sprint and have no testing or accessibility tickets for the next month, you can pause your subscription with one click inside your Stripe billing portal. Your remaining billing cycle pauses until you're ready to resume.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- FAQ 2 -->
      <div class="p-6 rounded-2xl bg-dark-800/60 border border-dark-700/80">
        <h4 class="text-base sm:text-lg font-bold text-white mb-2">Why wouldn't I just hire a full-time Senior SDET?</h4>
        <p class="text-sm text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
          Recruiting a senior QA engineer takes 2 to 4 months and averages $180k–$220k in base salary plus benefits, equity, and recruiting fees. Moreover, many companies don't need 40 hours/week of continuous architecture once the system is stable. Our subscription gives you senior-level execution on demand at a fraction of the cost.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- FAQ 3 -->
      <div class="p-6 rounded-2xl bg-dark-800/60 border border-dark-700/80">
        <h4 class="text-base sm:text-lg font-bold text-white mb-2">How fast do you deliver tickets in the async queue?</h4>
        <p class="text-sm text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
          On average, discrete tickets (a flaky test fix, a new E2E flow, an accessibility component remediation) are delivered in 24 to 48 hours. Larger epics (like migrating an entire test suite) are broken down into transparent 48-hour incremental milestones.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- FAQ 4 -->
      <div class="p-6 rounded-2xl bg-dark-800/60 border border-dark-700/80">
        <h4 class="text-base sm:text-lg font-bold text-white mb-2">What tech stacks and frameworks do you support?</h4>
        <p class="text-sm text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
          We specialize in modern web architectures: TypeScript, Playwright, Vitest, React, Next.js, Vue, Tailwind, and Node.js. For CI/CD, we support GitHub Actions, GitLab CI, CircleCI, and Docker.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- FAQ 5 -->
      <div class="p-6 rounded-2xl bg-dark-800/60 border border-dark-700/80">
        <h4 class="text-base sm:text-lg font-bold text-white mb-2">How does your accessibility testing meet US Federal requirements?</h4>
        <p class="text-sm text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
          We test against the exact statutory standard codified in the US DOJ ADA Title II Final Rule and HHS Section 504: <strong>WCAG 2.1 Level AA</strong>. We align test cases with the <strong>DHS Section 508 ICT Testing Baseline</strong>, covering static DOM checks (@axe-core), keyboard focus-trapping (ARIA APG), and real screen-reader audio feedback (Guidepup VoiceOver).
        </p>
      </div>

    </div>

  </div>
</section>
